---
title: Erosion by aggregation
---
Fire particles at a finished map and let them eat at its walls, so it looks more organic and keeps its structure [[t:191-197 s:21]].

## The rule
```text
start from a finished map
repeat for a number of particles:
    start a particle on a random open tile
    step at random until it stands on rock
    dig that tile
```

Each particle digs exactly one tile: the first rock its walk reaches from inside the open area [[c08:86-128 g]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=5 mid=1

## Controls
@@control iterations
How many particles are fired, each digging one tile [[c08:86-128]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

500 particles lift the floor share from random rooms’ {{c01.floor_share.median}} to {{c08.floor_share.median}}, and turn a map with no dead ends into one with {{c08.dead_ends.median}} at the median [[run:c01.floor_share.median c08.floor_share.median c08.dead_ends.median]]. Erosion only opens tiles next to open ones, and the map stays {{c08.regions.max}} region on every seed [[run:c08.regions.max]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

The demo’s walk has no cap [[c08:100-128]]. Ours has one, which {{c08.fails.guard-hit}} of these seeds reach [[run:c08.fails.guard-hit]].

